{"name":"Dance of the Goddesses","hex":"#e6d8cd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"},{"term":"goddesses","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of goddess"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goddesses"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"},{"title":"Goddess","blocks":[{"text":"A goddess is a female deity. In some faiths, a sacred female figure holds a central place in religious prayer and worship. For example, Shaktism, holds that the ultimate deity, the source of all reality, is Supreme Goddess (Mahamaya) and in some forms of Tantric Shaivism, the pair of Shiva and Shakti are the ultimate principle. Meanwhile, in Vajrayana Buddhism, ultimate reality is often seen as being composed of two principles depicted as two deities in union symbolising the non-duality of the two principles of perfect wisdom (female) and skillful compassion (male). A single figure in a monotheistic faith that is female may be identified simply as god because of no need to differentiate by gender or with a diminutive. An experiment to determine the effect of psychedelics on subjects composed of leaders from diverse religious groups revealed a general experience that the divine which the subjects encountered was feminine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg/330px-Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess","wikidata":"Q205985"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/GDC_onlywayaround.jpg/500px-GDC_onlywayaround.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/GDC_onlywayaround.jpg/500px-GDC_onlywayaround.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Members of an American jazz dance company perform a formal group routine in a concert dance setting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGDC_onlywayaround.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg/500px-Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg/1280px-Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg/500px-Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mesolithic dancers at Bhimbetka","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADancing_painting_at_Bhimbetk